- **Smart Warehousing Solutions**: IoT technology enables the development of smart warehouses equipped with sensors and connected devices that monitor inventory levels, track equipment performance, and optimize storage space. For example, automated inventory management systems can alert warehouse managers when stock levels fall below predefined thresholds, facilitating timely restocking and reducing the risk of stockouts.
- **Cold Chain Monitoring**: In industries where temperature-sensitive goods are involved, IoT devices can be employed to monitor and maintain optimal temperature conditions throughout the supply chain. Real-time temperature tracking ensures the integrity of perishable items and helps companies comply with regulatory requirements. Companies such as Maersk have implemented IoT solutions to enhance the visibility and reliability of their cold chain logistics.

